INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES
  ('efficiency-vs.-experience:-the-downside-of-self-service-kiosks-in-dining', 'Efficiency vs. Experience: The Downside of Self-Service Kiosks in Dining', 'Efficiency at What Cost? The Hidden Downsides of Self-Service Kiosks in Restaurants', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Efficiency at What Cost? The Hidden Downsides of Self-Service Kiosks in Restaurants"},{"type":"p","text":"In recent years, the fast-paced adoption of self-service kiosks in the restaurant industry has been praised for its potential to streamline operations and address staffing shortages. However, a recent study conducted by experts in food and beverage marketing has unveiled an unexpected drawback: the social dynamics of lines at automated kiosks can lead to a decrease in customer spending. This article explores the surprising downside of self-service kiosks and suggests ways that restaurants can mitigate these issues."},{"type":"p","text":"The Pressure of the Line"},{"type":"p","text":"When customers use self-service kiosks to place their orders, a common occurrence is the formation of lines behind them. According to the study, the presence of people waiting imposes an unspoken pressure on the customer using the kiosk to hurry through their decision-making process."},{"type":"p","text":"\"We found that when customers perceive that they are holding up the line, they feel rushed and tend to make quicker, less considered decisions,\" says one of the study’s authors."},{"type":"p","text":"This phenomenon leads customers to opt for familiar items they know well, rather than taking the time to browse through the menu and consider new or additional items. As a result, spending decreases because customers are not exploring the full range of options available to them."},{"type":"p","text":"A Psychological Battle"},{"type":"p","text":"To delve deeper into this issue, researchers conducted three experiments involving hundreds of participants who were asked to imagine themselves in various restaurant scenarios. Overwhelmingly, participants reported feeling pressured to order quickly when there was a visible queue behind them. This implicates a significant psychological component: the fear of social judgment from those waiting."},{"type":"p","text":"\"As people generally aim to be considerate of others, they inadvertently end up rushing their own experience, possibly missing out on items they might have enjoyed, ergo contributing to lower overall sales for the restaurant,\" explained the study."},{"type":"p","text":"The Single Line Solution"},{"type":"p","text":"One proposed solution to alleviate this pressure is the implementation of a single queue that serves multiple kiosks. This arrangement distributes the wait time among all customers, rather than placing the full burden on the individual currently placing their order."},{"type":"p","text":"With multiple kiosks fed by a single line, customers don’t feel as targeted or stressed about holding up others. This not only reduces the emotional rush experienced by the person at the kiosk but also boosts their confidence to explore the menu more thoroughly."},{"type":"p","text":"Systemic Communication"},{"type":"p","text":"Another effective fix involves kiosk interface design. Researchers suggest that a simple pop-up message could significantly mitigate perceived pressure. This message would communicate that the restaurant takes full responsibility for any delays during the ordering process, reassuring customers that they are not at fault for the longer wait times."},{"type":"p","text":"When customers feel that the blame for any hold-up doesn''t lie on their shoulders, they can take their time, potentially increasing both customer satisfaction and sales. The psychological effect of feeling supported by the business can create a more relaxed and enjoyable ordering experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Broader Implications"},{"type":"p","text":"The study’s findings highlight an important aspect of the evolving intersection between technology and consumer behavior. For restaurant owners considering the transition to automated systems, it''s critical to understand these social dynamics to avoid unintended consequences."},{"type":"p","text":"\"As we seek to make the dining experience more efficient through self-service technology, we must not overlook the human factors at play,\" advises the research team. \"Design choices that address these social dynamics can lead to a more effective and customer-friendly self-service system.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Conclusion"},{"type":"p","text":"While self-service kiosks offer numerous advantages, such as improved operational efficiency and a solution to staffing issues, restaurants must be mindful of the hidden challenges these systems can introduce. By adopting strategies like single lines to serve multiple kiosks and using supportive messaging within the interface, restaurants can enhance the customer experience, leading to increased satisfaction and spending."},{"type":"p","text":"Incorporating these elements into the design and layout of self-service systems addresses both operational and psychological aspects, ensuring that the benefits of automation do not come at the cost of customer engagement and revenue."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_1c1013650940453e97911d25ba9e7a4d~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/Blog%202%20(8).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-09-03', 'published'),
  ('adulterated-avocado-oil:-spotting-the-signs-of-contamination-with-cheap-oils', 'Adulterated Avocado Oil: Spotting the Signs of Contamination with Cheap Oils', 'Introduction to Avocado Oil: Understanding Its Purity', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Introduction to Avocado Oil: Understanding Its Purity"},{"type":"p","text":"Avocado oil has surged in popularity in recent years, praised for its heart-healthy properties and mild flavor. However, recent scientific analysis reveals that much of the avocado oil available in stores is adulterated, misleading consumers who believe they are purchasing pure avocado oil."},{"type":"p","text":"Rampant Adulteration in Avocado Oil"},{"type":"p","text":"UC-Davis Study Reveals Grim Findings"},{"type":"p","text":"Scientists at the University of California at Davis conducted comprehensive tests on avocado oil samples and identified alarming levels of adulteration and mislabeling. The study revealed that 21 out of 36 bottles tested, approximately two-thirds, were found to be adulterated with cheaper seed and vegetable oils, and sometimes oils that could pose risks to individuals with food sensitivities."},{"type":"p","text":"Retailers Involved in Selling Adulterated Products"},{"type":"p","text":"The study pointed fingers at some of the largest retail chains in the U.S. and Canada, including Walmart, Sam’s Club, Kroger, and Safeway. These retailers did not respond to requests for comments, while others dispute the findings or cite supply chain complexities."},{"type":"p","text":"How Cheap Avocado Oil is Made"},{"type":"p","text":"Unrefined vs. Refined Avocado Oil"},{"type":"p","text":"The quality of avocado oil varies widely depending on the type of processing:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Unrefined Oils: These are typically labeled as virgin or extra virgin. They are minimally processed, preserving more nutrients and a green tint.","Refined Oils: Highly processed using methods like bleaching and deodorizing, these oils are less nutrient-dense and neutral in flavor."]},{"type":"p","text":"The Risks of Misleading Labels"},{"type":"p","text":"Adulterated oils not only deceive consumers but also pose health risks, particularly for those with food sensitivities. More concerning is the use of cheaper oils like sunflower, safflower, and canola by unscrupulous suppliers looking to profit."},{"type":"p","text":"Suppliers Selling Fake Avocado Oil"},{"type":"p","text":"According to industry experts, the pervasive adulteration isn''t a secret. Ben Barnard, founder and chairman of AvoPacific, a leading avocado oil producer, noted that prices offered by some competitors are suspiciously low, indicating potential adulteration to cut costs."},{"type":"p","text":"The Adulterated Avocado Oil Brands"},{"type":"p","text":"In response to calls for transparency, UC-Davis disclosed the brands that failed their tests. Retailers implicated include Walmart, Trader Joe’s, Aldi, Metro, Meijer, and Kroger. The most frequent adulterants identified were sunflower, safflower, canola, and soybean oils."},{"type":"p","text":"Examples of Adulterated Products"},{"type":"p","text":"Among the worst offenders was Stop & Shop’s store-brand “extra-virgin” avocado oil, which despite its high price, was found to contain oils that were not even avocado oil."},{"type":"p","text":"Retailers’ Reactions to Study Findings"},{"type":"p","text":"Most retailers, such as Trader Joe’s and Metro, insist their products meet quality standards based on certifications from suppliers and third-party labs. However, these guarantees are often based on outdated or incomplete testing and do not account for the findings from the recent UC-Davis study."},{"type":"p","text":"Statements from Retailers"},{"type":"p","text":"Retailers provided mixed responses:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Stop & Shop: Claimed they no longer used the implicated supplier and have switched to routine testing.","Trader Joe’s: Stated reliance on industry-standard testing but did not retest old batches.","Metro: Asserted compliance based on tests from their own records and recent government inspections."]},{"type":"p","text":"The Need for Better Oversight and Independent Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Selina Wang, the UC-Davis scientist leading the research, emphasized that retailers should not rely solely on supplier certifications, advocating for routine independent testing to validate product integrity. This measure would be a significant step toward ensuring consumers get what they believe they are buying."},{"type":"p","text":"The rampant adulteration of avocado oil is an issue that needs industry-wide attention and stricter regulatory oversight. Consumers deserve transparency and accuracy in food labeling, and it’s imperative that both retailers and suppliers work together to ensure the products on store shelves meet the quality promised on their labels."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_7d16ba6d52fe4fc988a7800bf17914a1~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/Blog%201%20(4).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-09-02', 'published'),
  ('dining-out-with-a-twist:-why-self-service-kiosks-might-lead-to-healthier-orders', 'Dining Out with a Twist: Why Self-Service Kiosks Might Lead to Healthier Orders', 'Self-Service Kiosks Prompt Rushed Decisions and Familiar Choices', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Self-Service Kiosks Prompt Rushed Decisions and Familiar Choices"},{"type":"p","text":"According to a recent study, restaurant customers who order from self-service kiosks often feel rushed when there''s a line forming behind them, leading to hurried decisions and a tendency to stick to familiar menu items rather than trying something new. This revelation highlights a significant drawback of the self-service system that many eateries have recently adopted."},{"type":"p","text":"Single Line Approach Could Alleviate Customer Pressure"},{"type":"p","text":"Our findings indicate that businesses can reduce the pressure felt by customers and enhance their overall satisfaction by revamping their ordering system. One effective solution is to have a single line of waiting customers lead to multiple kiosks, rather than each kiosk having its own dedicated line. This approach ensures that customers feel less responsible for holding up the line, thereby providing them with a more relaxed ordering experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Experts in Food and Beverage Marketing Weigh In"},{"type":"p","text":"As experts in food and beverage marketing with a focus on self-service technology, we have observed a rising trend among restaurants to implement automated processes. This trend aims to streamline ordering and address staffing shortages, ultimately placing more control in the hands of customers. However, an unintended consequence of this shift is the added pressure customers feel to expedite their orders, resulting in less thoughtful choices and lower spending."},{"type":"p","text":"Three Experiments Highlight Customer Behavior"},{"type":"p","text":"To delve deeper into this issue, we conducted three experiments involving hundreds of participants. These experiments required participants to imagine waiting in line at a restaurant in different scenarios. The results confirmed that the presence of a queue led most people to feel pressured to order quickly. This pressure resulted in hastier decisions and reduced overall spending."},{"type":"p","text":"Mitigating the Pressure: Two Effective Solutions"},{"type":"p","text":"The experiments revealed two potential strategies for mitigating this pressure. Firstly, creating a single line that serves multiple kiosks can distribute the waiting time more evenly and reduce individual stress. Secondly, displaying a pop-up message on the kiosk interface, assuring customers that the business takes full responsibility for any service delays, can also alleviate the perceived need to rush."},{"type":"p","text":"Implications for Effective Self-Service Design"},{"type":"p","text":"Our research highlights the social dynamics at play in self-service ordering systems and offers valuable insights for designing a more effective and customer-friendly process. It alerts restaurant owners to the potential unintended consequences associated with the transition to automated technology and underscores the importance of thoughtful system redesigns to enhance customer experience and satisfaction."},{"type":"p","text":"The findings of this study suggest that while self-service kiosks can address certain operational challenges, they must be implemented in a way that considers the psychological and social dynamics of the customer experience. By doing so, restaurants can better navigate the complexities of automated ordering systems and ultimately drive more thoughtful purchases and higher customer satisfaction."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_478a36e6dc56440cb01f34cba777d0ee~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/Blog%202%20(6).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-08-30', 'published'),
  ('tech-trends-driving-the-future-of-the-restaurant-industry', 'Tech Trends Driving the Future of the Restaurant Industry', 'Revolutionizing Restaurant Management: The Technological Transformation', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Revolutionizing Restaurant Management: The Technological Transformation"},{"type":"p","text":"In the fast-paced and highly competitive restaurant industry, efficiency is the bedrock of success. Multi-unit restaurant managers face the daunting task of maintaining high standards across various locations. However, recent advances in restaurant technology - particularly the Internet of Things (IoT), Artificial Intelligence (AI), and robotics - are revolutionizing how these managers can achieve operational efficiency. These cutting-edge technologies streamline daily routines and enhance overall performance, offering innovative solutions to the challenges of multi-unit restaurant operations."},{"type":"p","text":"IoT for Real-Time Monitoring and Control"},{"type":"p","text":"The Internet of Things (IoT) refers to the network of interconnected devices that communicate and share data. In restaurant management, IoT significantly boosts efficiency through real-time monitoring and control of various operational aspects."},{"type":"ul","items":["Smart Kitchen Equipment: IoT-enabled kitchen appliances can monitor their performance, track usage patterns, and send alerts when maintenance is needed. This proactive maintenance approach reduces downtime and prevents unexpected equipment failures.","Temperature Monitoring: IoT sensors can monitor refrigeration units and other temperature-sensitive areas in real-time, ensuring food is stored at safe temperatures. Automated alerts notify managers of deviations, allowing quick corrective actions to prevent food spoilage and ensure safety.","Inventory Management: Smart inventory systems track stock levels in real-time, automatically reorder supplies when they run low, and even predict future needs based on historical data. This reduces waste and ensures that each unit always has the necessary ingredients."]},{"type":"p","text":"AI for Data-Driven Decision-Making"},{"type":"p","text":"Artificial Intelligence (AI) harnesses the power of machine learning and advanced algorithms to analyze large datasets, identify patterns, and make predictions. AI can be a game-changer in several key areas for multi-unit restaurant managers."},{"type":"ul","items":["Customer Insights: AI can analyze customer data to provide deep insights into preferences, spending habits, and feedback. This information can be used to personalize marketing efforts, optimize menu offerings, and enhance the overall customer experience.","Demand Forecasting: AI-powered tools can predict future demand based on historical sales data, seasonal trends, and external factors such as local events or weather conditions. Accurate demand forecasting helps managers make informed decisions about staffing, inventory, and promotions, leading to more efficient operations.","Labour Optimization: AI can analyze labor data to optimize scheduling, ensuring that each location is appropriately staffed based on predicted demand. This reduces labor costs and prevents overstaffing, enhancing employee satisfaction and customer service."]},{"type":"p","text":"Robotics for Streamlined Operations"},{"type":"p","text":"Robotics technology is making significant strides in the restaurant industry, offering innovative solutions to enhance efficiency and consistency in daily operations."},{"type":"ul","items":["Automated Food Preparation: Robotic systems can handle repetitive and time-consuming tasks such as chopping vegetables, assembling dishes, and even cooking certain menu items. This speeds up food preparation and ensures consistent quality across all units.","Service Robots: Robotic servers and bussers can assist with delivering food to tables, clearing dishes, and even interacting with customers in a fun and engaging way. By automating these tasks, human staff can focus on providing personalized service and improving the overall dining experience.","Cleaning and Sanitation: Robotic cleaning systems maintain high levels of cleanliness and hygiene, crucial in a post-pandemic world. These robots can clean floors, sanitize surfaces, and even wash dishes, ensuring a safe and spotless environment with minimal human intervention."]},{"type":"p","text":"Leveraging Today’s Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Integrating IoT, AI, and robotics into multi-unit restaurant operations represents a significant leap forward in achieving operational efficiency. By leveraging these advanced technologies, restaurant managers gain real-time insights, make data-driven decisions, and automate routine tasks, contributing to smoother, more efficient daily operations."},{"type":"p","text":"Embracing these technological advancements enhances efficiency, improves the overall customer experience, reduces operational costs, and supports sustainable growth. As the restaurant industry continues to evolve, staying ahead of the curve with the latest technology is essential for maintaining a competitive edge and achieving long-term success."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_5c604627dafc474e8c22bb7d9db9618a~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/News%20-%20Aug%2029.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-08-29', 'published'),
  ('leveraging-linkedin-for-restaurant-success', 'Leveraging LinkedIn for Restaurant Success', 'LinkedIn Advertising: Reaching Your Target Audience', '[{"type":"h2","text":"LinkedIn Advertising: Reaching Your Target Audience"},{"type":"p","text":"In the modern era of digital marketing, restaurants are constantly seeking innovative ways to enhance their online presence and gain competitive advantage. Surprisingly, one of the most effective tools is often overlooked, LinkedIn. While many restaurateurs rely heavily on platforms like Facebook and Instagram, LinkedIn offers unique opportunities that shouldn''t be underestimated."},{"type":"p","text":"Business Owners Turning to LinkedIn"},{"type":"p","text":"Owners and operators are increasingly using LinkedIn to improve community engagement, gain industry visibility, and foster professional relationships. More than just a networking site, LinkedIn has become a crucial element in digital marketing strategies for restaurants, enhancing recruitment efforts, brand building, and even customer conversion rates."},{"type":"p","text":"What is LinkedIn?"},{"type":"p","text":"LinkedIn is a distinctive social media platform focused on professional networking. With millions of members globally, it provides an excellent venue for connecting with other industry professionals, potential employees, and customers. Unlike other social media platforms, LinkedIn is designed to build professional relationships and nurture collaborative business opportunities."},{"type":"p","text":"The Professional Edge"},{"type":"p","text":"LinkedIn''s professional focus makes it an ideal space for restaurants aiming to strengthen their industry presence and make meaningful connections."},{"type":"p","text":"10 Ways LinkedIn Marketing Strategies Can Drive Restaurant Business"},{"type":"p","text":"1\\. Create a Detailed Company Page"},{"type":"p","text":"Start by creating a comprehensive company page. Highlight your restaurant''s culture, mission, vision, and community impact. Share employee testimonials to attract potential workers and partners."},{"type":"p","text":"2\\. Nurture Industry Connections"},{"type":"p","text":"LinkedIn offers direct access to influencers, critics, and food bloggers. It’s also an ideal way to research your competitors and join industry-specific groups for trends and insights."},{"type":"p","text":"3\\. Prioritize Customer Conversions"},{"type":"p","text":"Ensure easy conversion paths on your LinkedIn page. Include links to your website, online ordering system, and other social media accounts to facilitate customer engagement."},{"type":"p","text":"4\\. Consider the Visual Component"},{"type":"p","text":"Use striking visuals to keep followers engaged. Share high-quality images of your menu offerings, seasonal dishes, and promotions. Visual content is vital for making an impact on LinkedIn."},{"type":"p","text":"5\\. Recruit Top Talent"},{"type":"p","text":"Utilize LinkedIn for cost-effective recruitment. Post job openings, call for applicants, and search for potential candidates based on relevant criteria. Convey your restaurant as a desirable place of employment."},{"type":"p","text":"6\\. Answer Questions via LinkedIn Q&A"},{"type":"p","text":"Establish thought leadership by participating in LinkedIn''s Q&A forums. Answer questions on topics such as recipes, food ingredients, and restaurant management to boost your authority."},{"type":"p","text":"7\\. Join Discussion Groups"},{"type":"p","text":"Join relevant LinkedIn groups to gain industry insights and make valuable connections with other chefs, owners, and operators. Groups like the National Restaurant Association and Catering Professionals offer useful perspectives and networking opportunities."},{"type":"p","text":"8\\. Encourage Customer Reviews"},{"type":"p","text":"Customer reviews are essential. Encourage patrons to leave feedback on LinkedIn to build credibility and attract new customers."},{"type":"p","text":"9\\. Consider Using LinkedIn Ads"},{"type":"p","text":"Leverage LinkedIn’s targeted ad campaigns to reach a focused audience. These ads can be tailored based on demographic factors such as industry, job title, and location."},{"type":"p","text":"10\\. Track Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Utilize LinkedIn''s analytics feature to monitor page visits and content performance. Refine your strategies based on these insights to improve engagement and reach."},{"type":"p","text":"Implementing LinkedIn Marketing Strategies for Your Restaurant"},{"type":"p","text":"Integrating LinkedIn into your digital marketing strategy can significantly benefit your restaurant. From promoting your brand to recruiting talent, LinkedIn offers a plethora of opportunities. For those unsure where to begin, collaborating with a third-party digital marketing provider can help maximize the benefits of this powerful platform."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_9abfceaf29e94240a2836bec3d3577f1~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1281,al_c,q_90/colleagues-playing-digital-devices-coffee-shop.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-08-28', 'published'),
  ('why-contactless-payments-are-more-than-just-a-fad', 'Why Contactless Payments Are More Than Just a Fad', 'The Convenience of Contactless Ordering: A New Era for Diners', '[{"type":"h2","text":"The Convenience of Contactless Ordering: A New Era for Diners"},{"type":"p","text":"As the pandemic swept across the globe, it forced numerous industries to re-evaluate how they conducted their business. The restaurant industry was no exception. Quickly adopting contactless ordering and payment systems, restaurants found that their patrons, young and old alike, embraced these technologies wholeheartedly. Fast-food and coffee chains have notably benefited from self-service and contactless ordering solutions, providing customers with a convenient and efficient way to purchase and pay for food, all while avoiding long lines. Fast-casual and dine-in restaurants were not far behind in this transition."},{"type":"p","text":"The introduction of contactless technology has not only improved the customer experience but also addressed managerial concerns related to labor and supply chain shortages, lockdowns, and delivery challenges. Integrated software solutions across restaurants'' Point of Sale (POS) touchpoints provide real-time transaction tracking, simplifying reconciliation processes."},{"type":"p","text":"The Benefits of Contactless Dining"},{"type":"p","text":"The pandemic has accelerated the adoption of digital ordering and payment technologies in the restaurant industry. Implementing these technologies enables guests to communicate, order, and pay for their meals using devices like mobile apps or online ordering platforms, making the dining experience more convenient and streamlined."},{"type":"p","text":"Contactless Ordering"},{"type":"p","text":"The ability to place orders without interacting with wait staff has emerged as a significant asset in the restaurant sector. Utilizing QR codes, customers can access digital menus on their mobile devices, allowing for dynamic menu updates in real-time, whether to highlight daily specials or adjust for inventory shortages. This system simplifies the ordering process and can lead to increased customer visits and sales."},{"type":"p","text":"Branded Mobile Apps"},{"type":"p","text":"Custom mobile apps have proven to be a valuable investment for many restaurants, enhancing brand visibility and helping them stay competitive. These apps facilitate menu browsing, advance ordering, and payments. Features such as GPS tracking for easy restaurant location, various payment options, reservation systems, integrated loyalty programs, order tracking, promotions, push notifications, and customer support make branded apps indispensable. Unlike third-party providers, custom apps allow restaurants to manage customer relationships directly, thus fostering a loyal customer base."},{"type":"p","text":"Online Ordering Software"},{"type":"p","text":"While third-party delivery apps revolutionized food ordering, their high fees often eroded restaurant profits. Restaurants that developed their online ordering platforms have discovered that they can generate significant sales without depending on third-party services. Customers now expect online ordering availability and prefer ordering directly from restaurant-branded websites. When integrated with POS systems, these platforms streamline order processing, reduce manual errors, and minimize food waste. Additionally, they offer powerful tools for tracking customer data, opening doors to targeted marketing and engagement efforts."},{"type":"p","text":"Self-Service Kiosks"},{"type":"p","text":"Self-service kiosks have evolved beyond their initial uses in industries like travel. Given current labor challenges and increasing consumer demand for self-service options, kiosks are becoming vital in the restaurant sector. These kiosks extend the POS system, ensuring a seamless customer experience whether the order is placed online, via an app, or on-site. Studies show that customers often spend more when ordering from a kiosk, especially when the menu design includes enticing upselling opportunities."},{"type":"p","text":"Branded Digital Gift Cards"},{"type":"p","text":"Digital gift cards are gaining traction, evidenced by various studies indicating that a significant number of respondents load gift cards into mobile or digital wallets. Usage of digital wallets is on the rise, with digital card sales typically accounting for a substantial portion of retail revenue during holidays. These cards are also popular for personal budgeting and special occasions throughout the year. Registering gift cards online allows businesses to gather customer data and engage with them through targeted promotions. The advance revenue from gift card purchases and the additional spending that often occurs when the cards are redeemed further benefit businesses."},{"type":"p","text":"Contactless technology aligns seamlessly with the modern consumer''s desire for personalized experiences, autonomy, and convenience. Retaining existing customers is becoming increasingly challenging, given the myriad of options available today. Technologies such as online shopping, mobile payments, and self-service kiosks have captivated a generation, ensuring that contactless solutions remain a permanent and influential fixture in the restaurant industry."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_964bee31daae4e61945d5060bcfcbb45~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/Blog%201%20(4).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-08-27', 'published'),
  ('the-future-of-dining:-ai-and-automation-revolutionizing-restaurants', 'The Future of Dining: AI and Automation Revolutionizing Restaurants', 'Automated Reservations and Seamless Service: Reducing Wait Times and Enhancing Efficiency', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Automated Reservations and Seamless Service: Reducing Wait Times and Enhancing Efficiency"},{"type":"p","text":"The full-service restaurant industry is undergoing a significant transformation as artificial intelligence (AI) and automation are beginning to refine multiple aspects of dining. From enhancing the customer experience to optimizing kitchen operations, these advancements are providing more than just an upgrade, they’re becoming essential for survival in the competitive restaurant world."},{"type":"p","text":"Envisioning the Full-Service Restaurant Journey"},{"type":"p","text":"Today’s diners expect personalized experiences, and while the concept is not new, AI is rapidly accelerating its evolution. By analyzing customer data, AI can deliver unprecedented levels of personalization."},{"type":"p","text":"Imagine a dining journey where AI enhances every aspect. After booking a reservation, the system recognizes returning guests, welcomes them by name, and offers personalized dining suggestions based on their preferences. This kind of individualized attention isn’t just a luxury, it’s becoming a crucial part of the dining experience."},{"type":"p","text":"AI can also entice customers by sending personalized offers and promotions. For instance, frequent weekend diners might receive a special discount for themed nights. When customers arrive, they are greeted by name, and servers, aided by AI, have instant access to dining histories. Favorite dishes and preferred seating arrangements are prearranged, offering a seamless dining experience."},{"type":"p","text":"These personalized touches foster loyalty and make each visit memorable. By integrating customer preferences and providing thoughtful surprises, restaurants ensure that every dining experience feels unique."},{"type":"p","text":"The Secret Ingredient in the Kitchen: AI Efficiency"},{"type":"p","text":"AI isn’t limited to the dining room; it’s revolutionizing kitchen operations as well. AI-powered systems optimize every part of food preparation, from inventory management to cooking times. Smart sensors can monitor equipment for potential failures and maintenance needs, reducing waste and enhancing safety."},{"type":"p","text":"Moreover, AI improves workforce scheduling by predicting demand, thereby creating optimal staff schedules. Wearables like smartwatches provide crew members with reminders and guidance, streamlining kitchen operations. These technologies boost efficiency, enhancing both customer experience and restaurant profitability."},{"type":"p","text":"From Order to Table: AI Delivers Precision"},{"type":"p","text":"In the fast-paced world of restaurant kitchens, precision is key. AI-powered cameras are now ensuring that every order is prepared exactly as requested before it leaves the kitchen, enhancing the dining experience and reducing food waste."},{"type":"p","text":"AI’s role in food safety extends beyond the kitchen. By monitoring temperatures and conditions throughout the supply chain, AI helps prevent foodborne illnesses and tracks food traceability and expiration dates. AI can also adapt supply orders in real-time, managing stock levels to prevent shortages, or creatively suggesting daily specials with excess ingredients."},{"type":"p","text":"Innovating Restaurant Planning and Development"},{"type":"p","text":"AI is also transforming how restaurants plan, develop, and test new concepts. Digital twins, or virtual models of establishments, allow owners to experiment with layouts and staffing levels to find optimal configurations without disrupting daily operations."},{"type":"p","text":"AI-driven simulations enhance employee training by providing immersive experiences that quickly bring new hires up to speed. This reduces training costs and ensures staff are well-prepared for their roles."},{"type":"p","text":"The Road Ahead: A New Era for Full-Service Restaurants"},{"type":"p","text":"The full-service restaurant industry is just beginning to explore the possibilities of AI. As the technology matures, even more innovative applications will emerge. Envision a “restaurant brain” that coordinates everything from reservations to to-go orders, always optimizing for the best possible experience for customers and staff."},{"type":"p","text":"While there are concerns that AI might replace human workers, it’s more about using technology to gain an industry advantage. Some jobs may evolve, but new roles will also emerge. Restaurants should focus on training and upskilling staff to adapt to this tech-driven landscape."},{"type":"p","text":"Investing in AI isn’t just an upgrade; it’s a strategic move towards a sustainable and prosperous future. The implementation of advanced technologies enhances customer experiences, drives efficiency, and improves profitability, marking the dawn of a new era for full-service restaurants."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_9a39108df16c4fa7b27fd72eea9b733c~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/Blog%201%20(3).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-08-26', 'published'),
  ('combining-delivery-orders-results-in-extended-times,-poorer-quality', 'Combining Delivery Orders Results in Extended Times, Poorer Quality', 'When Faster Isn’t Better: The Hidden Costs of Bundled Deliveries', '[{"type":"h2","text":"When Faster Isn’t Better: The Hidden Costs of Bundled Deliveries"},{"type":"p","text":"Secret shoppers in a study from Intouch Insight were far less satisfied when their meal arrived after others were dropped off along the way, a common practice for apps like DoorDash, Uber Eats, and Grubhub. This story is part of a series based on The Path to Third-Party Excellence, an upcoming secret shopper study from Intouch Insight conducted exclusively for Restaurant Business and its sister publications CSP Daily News and Nation''s Restaurant News."},{"type":"p","text":"Impact on Delivery Times and Food Quality"},{"type":"p","text":"Third-party delivery providers’ practice of bundling multiple orders in one trip slows delivery times and hurts customer satisfaction, according to the Intouch Insight report. The study, which used secret shoppers to place 600 delivery orders from restaurants and convenience stores across the U.S., illustrates the drawbacks of order batching, a tactic that has long been used by restaurant delivery apps but is rarely discussed openly."},{"type":"p","text":"The Scope of the Study"},{"type":"p","text":"The Intouch Insight shoppers were instructed to order from whatever establishment they wished, but they couldn’t use a paid membership or pay extra for a direct delivery. The results showed that 12% of orders were picked up and delivered by a courier who first made other drop-offs along the way. Shoppers were notified within the app when this was the case."},{"type":"p","text":"Longer Last Leg and Compromised Quality"},{"type":"p","text":"Per the results, the last leg of a batched delivery took more than 42 minutes to complete, on average, or more than 13 minutes longer than orders that traveled directly to the customer. This delay negatively impacted the food, with the temperature correct only 77% of the time for batched deliveries compared to 95% for direct deliveries. Customer satisfaction also took a hit, with overall satisfaction at 79% for batched orders, 10 points lower than for nonstop orders."},{"type":"p","text":"Frequency of Batching by App"},{"type":"p","text":"According to the Intouch Insight results, batching was fairly common, though the frequency differed by app: 19% of orders placed with Uber Eats were part of a batched delivery compared to 12% for DoorDash and 5% for Grubhub."},{"type":"p","text":"Responses from Delivery Apps"},{"type":"p","text":"A DoorDash representative said several factors dictate when orders are batched but did not elaborate. Uber CEO Dara Khosrowshahi previously mentioned that the company uses artificial intelligence to determine when to bundle orders. Both representatives emphasized that batching is designed to get customers their orders faster during busy periods."},{"type":"p","text":"A Grubhub spokesperson said 86% of the company’s overall orders arrive on time but did not provide a figure for batched orders."},{"type":"p","text":"The Challenges for Restaurants"},{"type":"p","text":"“\\[Batched delivery\\] is not working for the customer,” said Sarah Beckett, director of marketing at Intouch Insight. “But also, the other element of it for the restaurant or the convenience store is, how do they protect their reputation, their brand, when some of this stuff is really taken out of their control?”"},{"type":"p","text":"One suggested solution is to invest in better packaging to ensure food stays fresh during trips with multiple stops."},{"type":"p","text":"The Bigger Picture"},{"type":"p","text":"These findings highlight another potential pain point in the relationship between restaurants and third-party delivery providers. Though the apps have become an important revenue channel for many operators since the pandemic, some complain about high delivery commissions, lack of data on their delivery customers, and a loss of control once an order leaves their store."},{"type":"p","text":"Yet, the results also show that consumers are generally quite happy with the third-party delivery experience. Shoppers’ overall satisfaction with restaurant delivery across all three apps was 91%, a 4-point improvement from 2022, when Intouch Insight last measured it."},{"type":"p","text":"Conclusion"},{"type":"p","text":"As third-party delivery continues to grow, the industry must address the negative impacts of batching on both delivery times and food quality. Restaurants may need to find innovative ways to ensure their food arrives fresh, while the delivery apps must balance cost efficiency with customer happiness to maintain their share of this increasingly competitive market."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_3393f32bae4b4f66ac3a87eddadcd4d6~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/Blog%201%20(3).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-08-22', 'published');
